       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The maximum labeled dose is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, or 2,000 mg/day for extended-release.\n- A single 1700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per administration.\n- A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 850 mg PO twice daily with meals (1,700 mg/day total)\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 500 mg or 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- Another dose\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
